{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0057","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What are the two standard methods for supervised domain adaptation of neural networks discussed in the paper?","answer":"The two standard methods are fine tuning (training on source data then tuning on target data) and dual outputs (a shared input with separate source and target output layers)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0057","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What is identified as one of the state-of-the-art methods for supervised domain adaptation?","answer":"Feature augmentation is identified as one of the state-of-the-art methods for supervised domain adaptation."}
